  "id": "minimal-brain-dysfunction",
  "term": "minimal brain dysfunction",
  "definition": "Minimal brain dysfunction is an older diagnostic label that was used for children with hard-to-manage behavior before ADHD became the more established psychiatric term. In the source, it is described as a broad and poorly defined category that often did not clearly distinguish socially troublesome behavior from a smaller number of biologically based difficulties.",
